title Online Bookstore: Deployment Diagram
left to right direction
node "User device" {
  artifact "Web browser" as BR
}
node "Application host (provider TBD)\nNode.js runtime\nHTTPS terminated by the host" as APP {
  artifact "Express API (/api/*)\n+ reservation sweeper" as API
  artifact "React build (static files)" as WEB
}
database "MongoDB Atlas (tier TBD)\nreplica set, daily backup\nincludes GridFS images" as DB
cloud "Payment Gateway\n(sandbox / test mode)" as PG
cloud "Email Service\n(provider TBD)" as ES
cloud "Uptime monitor\n(tool TBD)" as UM
BR --> APP : HTTPS 443\nSPA files and /api calls
APP --> DB : MongoDB protocol over TLS
APP --> PG : HTTPS (create, verify, refund)
PG ..> APP : HTTPS webhook (signed)
APP --> ES : SMTP over TLS or HTTPS
UM --> APP : HTTPS GET /api/health\nevery 5 min or less
BR ..> PG : HTTPS hosted payment form
note bottom of APP
  One service serves both the API and the React build,
  so the browser sees a single origin (no CORS,
  first-party cookies) and one keep-alive target.
end note
@enduml
